"""
Silver table reconciliation:  core (read replica)  vs  core_tst_std001 (CDA)
=============================================================================

INPUTS - set in the "INPUTS (edit here)" block below.
         main({...}) can also be called with a dict of the same lower-case keys to override them.
  TABLE_NAMES      one schema.table per line. Optional key:  schema.table:key1|key2
  KEY_COLUMNS      default key for tables without their own key (optional)
  EXCLUDE_COLUMNS  extra columns to ignore. LOAD_DT and HASH_DIFF are ALWAYS excluded.
  FILTER_COLUMN    window column, default SYS_EFCTV_DT
  FILTER_MODE      MAX_CUTOFF: per table, cutoff = max(SYS_EFCTV_DT) of RR / CDA / MIN of both
                   (CUTOFF_FROM); both sides compared on (cutoff - WINDOW_HOURS, cutoff].
                   FIXED: FILTER_START / FILTER_END ('yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm:ss' | 'yyyy-MM-dd' | DAILY | blank)
                   Filter column missing in either table = whole data compared on BOTH sides.
  SAMPLE_ROWS      sample records stored per table

EXECUTION ORDER  tables that have the filter column on both sides run first, then the rest.
                 PARALLEL_TABLES tables run at the same time.

HOW DATA IS COMPARED (fast path first, detail only where needed)
  1 FINGERPRINT  one scan per side: count + 128-bit order-independent checksums of every row,
                 raw ("strict") and format-normalised. Equal -> table matches, no join needed.
  2 DUPLICATES   exact duplicate rows and duplicate keys from the cached 64-bit row/key hashes
                 (one shuffle of longs per side).
  3 BUCKETS      only if 1 differs: rows split into NUM_BUCKETS hash buckets (by key, or by row hash
                 when no key) and each bucket's checksum compared. Identical buckets = matched.
  4 DRILL-DOWN   full-record multiset compare, unmatched samples, key-level per-column value and
                 format checks, NULL/blank profile - only on rows in the differing buckets.
  Normalisation: whitespace, blank vs NULL, numeric scale, date/timestamp format, string<->typed cast.
  Every step is isolated: a failing step is logged as ERROR and the remaining steps still run;
  a failing table does not stop the other tables.

OUTPUT  (core_tst_std001.testing_sb, Delta, appended every run, created / extended automatically)
  recon_summary           one row per table per run
  recon_check_results     one row per finding, detailed comments
  recon_mismatch_samples  sample records: SRC_ONLY | TGT_ONLY | FORMAT_DIFF | DUP_KEY | DUP_ROW
  recon_summary_latest    view: latest run per table per day
  latest_run_ind = 'Y' only on the latest run of a table for each run_date; earlier runs that day -> 'N'
"""

